# Automation-Plus MCP-Server – Bewerbungs-Automation

## Relevante MCP-Server (Cursor Settings → MCP aktivieren)

| Server | Zweck | Typische Nutzung |
|--------|-------|------------------|
| **mcp-nocodb** | Tabellen, Records | Seed-Daten, Jobs, Matches, CRUD |
| **mcp-infra** | Infrastruktur | N8n-Workflows, Trigger, Status |
| **mcp-docker** | Container | N8n, NocoDB, Coolify-Container |
| **mcp-database** | PostgreSQL | NocoDB-Backend, direkte SQL-Abfragen |
| **mcp-hetzner** | Cloud-Server | Server-Status, SSH, Ressourcen |
| **mcp-grafana** | Dashboards | Metriken, Monitoring |
| **mcp-nextcloud** | Dateien | Workflow-Exports, Reports speichern |
| **mcp-gitops** | Repos | Workflow-JSON versionieren |
| **mcp-coolify** | Deployment | deploy_application, trigger_backup |
| **mcp-n8n** | Workflows | trigger_workflow, list_workflows |

## mcp-nocodb

- `nocodb_list_bases`, `nocodb_list_tables`
- `nocodb_create_record`, `nocodb_update_record`, `nocodb_delete_record`
- `nocodb_get_records`, `nocodb_search_records`
- **Einschränkung:** Schema nur in NocoDB-UI, nicht per MCP

## mcp-infra (inkl. N8n)

- Workflow-Trigger, Workflow-Status
- N8n-API-Operationen (falls verfügbar)
- Infrastruktur-Checks

## mcp-docker

- Container-Status (homestack-n8n, homestack-nocodb)
- Logs, Restart
- Coolify-Integration

## mcp-database

- PostgreSQL-Queries (NocoDB nutzt ggf. Postgres)
- Backup, Migrations

## mcp-hetzner

- Server <HETZNER_HOST> (hetzner)
- Ressourcen, Firewall

## Konfiguration

MCP-Server: `Desktop/01_Command_Center/03_Agents/06_mcp-config/mcp.json`  
Alle URLs: `https://mcp-*.automation-plus-ki.de/mcp`
